-A digitally controlled USB-C laboratory supply was developed from a charge-pump PFC resonant converter and supplied planar magnetics. The first prototype, V1, was used for circuit bring-up and control development. V2 integrated the MCU and associated circuitry on the converter PCB. The V3 edge-card layout was then developed to reduce the converter volume.
