 \section*{Preface and Project Contribution}
 \addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Preface and Project Contribution}
 
-This thesis was prepared at \department, Technical University of Denmark, for the \degreeprogramme. A USB-C laboratory power supply was built around a charge-pump PFC resonant converter. Its controller was developed for operation with a detachable load.
+This thesis was prepared at \department, Technical University of Denmark, for the \degreeprogramme. A USB-C power supply was built around a charge-pump PFC resonant converter. Its controller was developed for operation with a detachable load.
 
 The topology and planar-magnetic designs were supplied by earlier DTU work. In this project, the schematic and PCB were implemented, the supplied magnetics were integrated, and the MCU firmware was developed. The first prototype was brought up and tested on the manufactured V1.0 PCB with rework. Its later drawing corrections were documented in V1.1. Development then continued with the integrated V2 board. Preliminary powered V2 observations are reported separately in \cref{sec:res-v2-testing}. Appendix~\ref{app:provenance} identifies the inherited designs and the author's integration, control, and test work.
 
